From: Claude Assistant <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 23:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix intermittent 400 on assignment creation: scope subjects
 to teacher's class

Root cause: /subjects/ returned every subject in the school regardless of
class, so the teacher portal's Assignment/Lesson form let teachers pick a
subject belonging to a different class. The serializer correctly rejects
that cross-class combination, causing a 400 on POST /api/assignments/.

- SubjectViewSet now filters by ?school_class= query param
- fetchSubjects/loadSubjects accept and forward the teacher's class id
- TeacherPortal loads (and reloads) subjects scoped to the selected class
---
 backend/apps/subjects/views.py                           | 9 ++++++++-
 frontend/admin-dashboard/src/pages/teacher/Hooks.jsx     | 4 ++--
 .../admin-dashboard/src/pages/teacher/TeacherPortal.jsx  | 7 +++++--
 .../src/pages/teacher/Teacherportalservice.jsx           | 5 +++--
 4 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend/apps/subjects/views.py b/backend/apps/subjects/views.py
index 0fa99e6..371b7c0 100644
--- a/backend/apps/subjects/views.py
+++ b/backend/apps/subjects/views.py
@@ -6,4 +6,11 @@ from .serializers import SubjectSerializer
 class SubjectViewSet(ModelViewSet):
 
     queryset = Subject.objects.all().order_by("name")
-    serializer_class = SubjectSerializer
\ No newline at end of file
+    serializer_class = SubjectSerializer
+
+    def get_queryset(self):
+        queryset = super().get_queryset()
+        school_class = self.request.query_params.get("school_class")
+        if school_class:
+            queryset = queryset.filter(school_class_id=school_class)
+        return queryset
\ No newline at end of file
